.TH PREV 1 "2026-10-17" "prev 2.2.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prev \- view, mark up and sign PDFs and images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prev
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prev
is a document and image viewer and editor similar to macOS Preview. It
opens PDFs, images (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, AVIF, HEIC, TIFF, BMP, ICO, TGA,
PNM, QOI, JPEG 2000, OpenEXR, Radiance HDR and camera RAW), SVG drawings
and Markdown.
.PP
Each document opens in its own window; images given together share one
window. A single instance runs per user: running
.B prev
again opens the files in the running instance and exits.
.PP
The assistant, a chat panel beside a document, answers about the file
and works in it with prev's own tools. It talks to a model added in the
Assistant tab of Settings: a local model served by Ollama or another
OpenAI-compatible server, or a cloud model from Anthropic, OpenAI or
Google Gemini, whose API key is kept in the system keychain.
.PP
Edits to PDFs and images are saved in place a moment after they are
made. Before the first save, the original is kept in the version
history, from which the image inspector's Revert To restores it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp
Serve MCP on standard input and output, so an AI agent can control the
running prev, which starts if it is not running. prev asks the user before
an agent it has not seen gets to act; Settings turns this off and chooses
what else prev asks about.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat every following argument as a file, even if it starts with a dash.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/prev.toml
Settings, including where the files below are kept.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/prev/signatures
Saved signatures.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/prev/versions
Earlier versions of edited files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/prev/bookmarks.toml
PDF bookmarks.
.PP
API keys for the assistant's cloud models are kept in the Secret Service,
not in these files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where settings, data and the instance socket go, when set.
.SH NOTES
prev uses these programs when they are installed:
.B wl-copy
and
.B wl-paste
for copying and pasting images,
.B curl
for pictures dropped from a browser as a web address only, and the
.B libheif
library for HEIC and AVIF.
.SH SEE ALSO
The tour of every feature: https://prev.run/guide.html
